  "solution": {
    "text": "In o-nitrophenol, hydrogen of $\\mathrm{O}-\\mathrm{H}$ group and oxygen of nitro group form intramolecular hydrogen bonding producing a six membered ring structure while in $m$-nitrophenol, $p$-nitrophenol and phenol, intermolecular hydrogen bonding are present.\nThe structure is,\n<img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/bitsat/bJMHIfwCUYjejPxFDVsiw5tqm-7snTCelfdPxnxX7CE.original.fullsize.png\"/><br/>",
